==============================================================================
COUNT FINDING — funding_carry_fade_v1   (no scores, no percentiles)
==============================================================================
  rule             : |f| >= 0.0001 at the LAST funding print on or before the bar close   (frozen)
  direction        : f >= +0.0001 -> SHORT (fade rich long carry); f <= -0.0001 -> LONG
  barrier          : +1.5/-1.5 ATR, horizon 5, 25 bps, entry next_open, on the LINEAR daily series
  costs            : 25 bps round trip PLUS the funding actually paid over each hold
  hard gate        : >= 50 scored trades per symbol

  BTCUSDT  1,461 bars   setups  417   scoreable  417   entries   85   -> MEETS the 50-trade gate
  ETHUSDT  1,461 bars   setups  415   scoreable  415   entries   76   -> MEETS the 50-trade gate
  SOLUSDT  1,461 bars   setups  534   scoreable  531   entries  162   -> MEETS the 50-trade gate

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHERE THE SAMPLE GOES — the join, then the scheduler
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  BTCUSDT  4,383 funding prints; 1,461 of 1,461 bars joined a rate (no forward-fill)
           417 setups -> 85 contiguous runs (longest 66) -> 85 entries (6 long / 79 short)
           funding ADJUSTMENT to net R: -0.0153 on longs, +0.0153 on shorts
           (a short RECEIVES positive funding, so its net R rises; a long pays. Applied to observed AND every replicate.)
  ETHUSDT  4,383 funding prints; 1,461 of 1,461 bars joined a rate (no forward-fill)
           415 setups -> 76 contiguous runs (longest 96) -> 76 entries (8 long / 68 short)
           funding ADJUSTMENT to net R: -0.0115 on longs, +0.0115 on shorts
           (a short RECEIVES positive funding, so its net R rises; a long pays. Applied to observed AND every replicate.)
  SOLUSDT  4,458 funding prints; 1,461 of 1,461 bars joined a rate (no forward-fill)
           534 setups -> 162 contiguous runs (longest 86) -> 162 entries (65 long / 97 short)
           funding ADJUSTMENT to net R: -0.0032 on longs, +0.0032 on shorts
           (a short RECEIVES positive funding, so its net R rises; a long pays. Applied to observed AND every replicate.)

Rich funding PERSISTS for days, so the flags form long runs and
simulate_schedule takes one entry per run (slice 17 — the rule that
makes the rotation null valid). The gap between setups and entries
is that persistence, not a defect, and it is printed rather than
described so the control is not asked to explain it later.

